//! A board in an enclosure for the editor recipes. Its physical file, `enclosure_limits.physical.nsm`, states the
//! enclosure's limits as seven height-only keepouts (a floor clearance over the whole back, a lower limit near an
//! edge, a boss, a tab, a screw shank and two ribs on the front) and one keepout that forbids parts on the front.
//! The layout file puts one header on the back and two on the front, so the view has both faces to look at and
//! limits that overlap one another and the parts.

import std::parts::connector::{Header1x2, Header2x3}
import std::mfg::jlcpcb::TwoLayer

board Enclosed {
    .process: TwoLayer {
        .stackup.thickness &= 1.6mm
    }
    .front_a: Header1x2
    .back_a: Header1x2
    .front_b: Header2x3
}
